🛡️ End-to-End Credit Card Fraud Detection & Risk Scoring System
A production-grade, full-stack machine learning application built to detect fraudulent credit card transactions in real time. This project features a decoupled architecture separating a Scikit-Learn inference backend, a Flask REST API, an automated SQLite audit logging database, and an interactive Streamlit analyst dashboard.

🏗️ System Architecture
Plaintext
[Streamlit Analyst Dashboard (UI)]
         │ 
         ▼ (HTTP POST Request / Predict)
[Flask REST API Backend] ──> [Scikit-Learn Model & StandardScaler]
         │ 
         └──> [SQLite Audit Database (`transactions.db`)]
🚀 Key Features
Real-Time Risk Scoring: Streamlit sidebar interface allowing operators to either input custom transaction parameters or dynamically load verified historical fraud cases from the dataset.

Full-Feature Inference Pipeline: Evaluates all 30 transaction features (including Time, Amount, and 28 anonymized PCA components V1–V28) to capture hidden fraud patterns.

Tuned Decision Threshold: Optimized classification threshold set to 0.2 to effectively flag high-risk anomalies despite extreme class imbalance in financial transaction datasets.

Automated SQLite Audit Logging: Every scanned transaction automatically logs timestamps, input parameters, calculated fraud probabilities, binary predictions, and status classifications (LEGITIMATE / FRAUDULENT) into a persistent relational database.

Decoupled Architecture: Clean separation of concerns between frontend presentation, RESTful API routing, and database storage.

🧰 Tech Stack & Tools
Machine Learning & Preprocessing: Python, Scikit-Learn (Random Forest Classifier), Pandas, NumPy, Joblib, PCA feature transformation

Backend API: Flask, RESTful architecture, JSON payload handling

Database & Persistence: SQLite, Python sqlite3 driver, automated schema migrations

Frontend UI: Streamlit, interactive dataframes, dynamic metric counters

Development & Deployment Tools: VS Code, Git/GitHub, Virtual Environments (venv)

