⚙️ Installation & Local Setup
Clone the Repository:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/chinmaypatil7/Creditcard-FraudDetection.git
cd Creditcard-FraudDetection
Create and Activate a Virtual Environment:

Bash
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate     # On Windows PowerShell
Install Dependencies:

Bash
pip install flask streamlit scikit-learn pandas joblib
🖥️ Running the Application
Because this system uses a decoupled client-server architecture, both the backend API and the frontend dashboard must run concurrently.

Step 1: Start the Flask Backend API
Open your first terminal window, activate your virtual environment, and run:

Bash
python app/api.py
(The API will launch and listen for requests on [http://127.0.0.1:5000](http://127.0.0.1:5000))

Step 2: Launch the Streamlit Dashboard
Open a second terminal window, activate your virtual environment, and run:

Bash
streamlit run app/dashboard.py
(Streamlit will automatically open the interactive dashboard in your default web browser).

📊 How to Test the System
Manual Mode: Input custom transaction amounts and times via the Streamlit sidebar and click Score Transaction to test normal distribution routing.

Fraud Simulation Mode: Switch the sidebar toggle to "Load Real Fraud Case from Dataset" and click "Load & Score Fraud Sample" to feed a true historical anomaly with all 30 features into the pipeline, triggering a high-risk alert and updating your live SQLite audit log table instantly!

